    "body": "STOPPED: #1870 blocks this DXF catalog case. Claim released.\n\nThe three new catalog_plasma_profile tests fail on unchanged upstream/main 58cb641ca. The case is missing.\n\nThe build script imports the DXF and creates Plasma Profile. Generation then refuses the operation:\n\n    Plate profile: invalid machining parameters: this operation is checked against the stock 'Stock' and the chains of the DXF profile 'profile' (2 closed, 0 open) - there is no solid model; a toolpath from the chains of a DXF profile is not generated yet\n\nIssue #1870 already tracks this missing support. No duplicate issue is needed. A solid model substitute would not meet this issue.\n\nHeld work: https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/tree/issue/2873-plasma-profile at 15362444d6fac6001b75bed80df537e630f7dfc8. No PR is open.\n\nHunk review:\n- example_catalog.rs adds rebuild, regeneration, and plasma content pins to test this case.\n- build.camscript uses the named plasma machine and post to reproduce the requested DXF workflow.\n- model/generate.py creates original geometry and stores the outline first to test cut ordering.\n- model/profile.dxf records the generated plate and hole in millimetres.\n- docs/decisions/2873-plasma-profile.md records the dependency and rejected substitutes.\n\nThe three pins remain red. No project or NC file was produced. Mutation checks, the quick gate, clippy, and catalog checks were not run after the generation refusal.\n\nPR #2963 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n",
